  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nFor an open bound, the method moved the value the wrong way. It returned `bound - dir`, but `dir` is the direction to move back into the range. With `min_open=True` and `min=0`, a too-small value clamped to `-1`, which is outside the range. It now returns `bound + dir`, so that case gives `1`. The same fix applies to an open `max`.\n\nThe existing tests in `tests/test_types.py` only cover clamping with closed bounds, so none of them exercise this path.",
